No fee or separate permission is required for normal use of ADExMo, provided that the attribution, integrity, naming, and restriction clauses of this License are respected.

4. Attribution Requirement

Any public use, distribution, documentation, product, service, training material, article, repository, tool, or implementation that substantially incorporates, applies, describes, or reproduces ADExMo must include clear attribution to ADExMo and myobject srls.

The recommended attribution is:

"ADExMo (Action-Driven Execution Model) is an original model created by myobject srls."

Attribution must be reasonably visible in the relevant context, such as a README file, documentation page, license notice, project credits section, training material, or product documentation.

You must not remove, hide, alter, or obscure copyright notices, attribution notices, authorship statements, or license references included in the Official ADExMo Materials.

5. Protection of the ADExMo Name

The name "ADExMo" belongs to myobject srls as the name of the original model.

You may use the ADExMo name only to:

* identify the original model;
* state that a project, product, document, or tool is based on ADExMo;
* state that a project, product, document, or tool is compatible with ADExMo;
* provide proper attribution to myobject srls.

You may not use the ADExMo name in a way that:

* suggests official status, certification, endorsement, sponsorship, or approval by myobject srls without Official Approval;
* presents a modified or third-party system as the official ADExMo model;
* creates confusion between official and unofficial materials;
* uses ADExMo as the main name of a competing product, method, framework, or standard without Official Approval.

Terms such as "official ADExMo", "ADExMo certified", "ADExMo standard", "ADExMo approved", or similar claims may be used only with Official Approval.

6. No Rebranding or Misrepresentation

You may not copy, rename, rebrand, republish, or present ADExMo, the Official ADExMo Materials, or a substantially similar model as your own original system.

You may not:

* remove attribution and present ADExMo as authored by another person or organization;
* publish ADExMo under a different name as if it were a separate or independent model;
* incorporate ADExMo into another methodology, framework, or standard while hiding its origin;
* use the structure, terminology, documentation, or examples of ADExMo to create a confusingly similar competing model without attribution;
* claim ownership over the ADExMo model, its official documentation, or its official terminology.

7. Modifications, Extensions, Translations, and Integrations

You may apply ADExMo to your own projects and integrate ADExMo-based implementations into your own software, workflows, services, or client work.

However, you may not publish, distribute, or present any Modified ADExMo Material as part of ADExMo, as an official ADExMo version, or as an approved extension of ADExMo without Official Approval.

The following require Official Approval before publication or distribution:

* modified versions of the Official ADExMo Materials;
* public translations of the Official ADExMo Materials;
* official-looking extensions of the ADExMo model;
* alternative ADExMo specifications;
* modified ADRs presented as ADExMo ADRs;
* additions to the official ADExMo model, terminology, templates, or documentation path;
* public materials that imply they are maintained, approved, or endorsed by myobject srls.

Unofficial materials must be clearly identified as unofficial and must preserve attribution to ADExMo and myobject srls.

8. Compatible Implementations

You may create, use, distribute, or sell implementations, adapters, libraries, runtimes, tools, templates, examples, services, or products that are compatible with ADExMo.

Compatible implementations must not:

* modify the official meaning of ADExMo;
* claim official status without Official Approval;
* create confusion with Official ADExMo Materials;
* remove or hide attribution;
* present compatibility as certification or endorsement.

Acceptable wording includes:

* "based on ADExMo";
* "compatible with ADExMo";
* "implements ADExMo concepts";
* "unofficial ADExMo adapter".

Restricted wording without Official Approval includes:

* "official ADExMo implementation";
* "ADExMo certified";
* "approved by myobject srls";
* "the ADExMo standard" if used to describe an unofficial or modified version.

